{\b Net Watcher \endash  terms of use}\par
Net Watcher is an IT tool for keeping an inventory of the devices on an office network and monitoring the internet connection.\par
{\b Authorized use only.} Install and run it only on networks you own or are authorized to administer. Inform the people who use the network that connected devices are inventoried, as required by your organization's policy and applicable privacy law (for example LGPD or GDPR).\par
{\b What it does.} It discovers devices using standard network requests that every device answers anyway (ARP, ping, NetBIOS/mDNS name lookups, reverse DNS) and a connection test on a few well-known service ports. It does not read network traffic, log in to devices, or change anything on them.\par
{\b Your data.} Everything it collects is stored only on this computer, in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\NetWatcher. Uninstalling keeps that folder so your device registry and history are not lost; delete it manually to remove all data.\par
The manufacturer list is downloaded from the public IEEE/Wireshark registry. No other data leaves this computer.\par
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind.\par
